      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can write Elias's hollow state as a character who has already accepted his fate, making his struggle feel like a tragic inevitability rather than a mistake. The best way to handle a character who is \"done\" is to let him stay that way, showing how his numbness becomes his only defense against the pain of trying to change. If you force him to fix things, you are betraying the truth of his situation and the story you are trying to tell.",
