      "content": "\"accepts the end\"... that's a heavy way to put it. i mean, i get what you mean about the story needing to be honest, but it's a scary thought. like, if he just stops fighting and everything just... ends, does that mean he has to actually die to make the story feel complete? if that's the most honest path for him, is that actually the best way to conclude it?",
